{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL1vTxMDWvgvnoSoud2L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review close-out now ends `stale` instead of `failed` when the PR was merged or closed, or its branch is gone. `go test ./...` passes, and gofmt and go vet are clean on the changed packages.\n\n- **Detection:** before committing, the close-out reads the PR's state. It also treats a committer `ErrBranchGone` the same way, which covers the exact failure in the issue.\n- **Result:** a stale review commits nothing, adds no `ard:executor:failed`, posts no failure comment, and logs `review.pr_gone` with the state (`merged`, `closed` or `branch_gone`). The review itself is still posted on a best-effort basis, and an error posting it is logged and ignored.\n- **Fallbacks:** if the PR read itself fails, close-out carries on to the commit as before, and a missing branch there still gives `stale`. Any other commit error still fails the job.\n- **Worker jobs:** no change, as the plan decided. A worker's draft PR can't be merged while it runs, and a branch deleted mid-job stays a genuine failure.\n- **Gate 2:** no code change was needed, since stale jobs complete rather than fail. I added one sentence to `docs/runbooks/gate-2.md` saying so.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` has a new reviewer item 7 describing the case.\n- **Tests:** the new tests are in `internal/closeout/prgone_test.go` and cover merged-and-deleted, closed-unmerged, branch gone on an open PR, a `changes` verdict, a failed review post, other commit errors still failing, and a PR read error.\n\nThe main code change is in `internal/closeout/closeout.go`, with the stale plan in `plan.go`. The report is written to `.ard/184/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_read_input_tokens":63638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_toke